# Python Uses UV

When this repo uses Python (`pyproject.toml`, `*.py`, `uv.lock`): always use `uv` for package and environment management. Do not force uv on Node/Go/PHP-only repos.

## Required

- Use `uv add` to install dependencies.
- Use `uv remove` to uninstall dependencies.
- Use `uv sync` to install from lock/config state.
- Use `uv run` to execute Python tools and scripts.
- Use `uv venv` for virtual environment creation when needed.

## Do Not Use

- Do not use `pip install` directly.
- Do not use `python -m pip ...`.
- Do not use `pipenv`, `poetry`, or `conda` in this repository.

## Examples

```bash
# ✅ Correct
uv add fastapi pydantic
uv remove requests
uv sync
uv run pytest
uv run python main.py

# ❌ Incorrect
pip install fastapi
python -m pip install pydantic
poetry add fastapi
```
